  "changes": [
    "Reuse sand geometry and scalar height calculations across wind probes; skip loads which cannot reach a cohesive bond, retaining dry loads on wet supports.",
    "Use allocation-light water prediction and compact exact CPU sampling/neighbor queries.",
    "Evaluate foam air-exposure and solid probes on the GPU, included in the existing single packed readback.",
    "Reuse boundary gradients between GPU constraint passes; specialize draw-constant shader features.",
    "Pack field and flow inputs directly; skip water-blob fragments already hidden by the bulk surface.",
    "Estimate the next physics-step cost before dispatch to avoid overrunning the frame budget. Always execute at least one due step and retain simulation debt.",
    "Incrementally update local settling contact/column indices while preserving reference query order.",
    "Bound newly created settling subdivisions by world resolution; combine overlapping sub-resolution wind deposits without deleting grain mass or moisture. User-held, carved or pushed stock is protected."
  ],
  "effectiveChanges": "The largest reductions were sand wind/stress work in busy scenes, allocation-light water prediction, and packed field preparation. Component timings are combined-pass measurements, not isolated causal ablations.",
  "remainingWork": [
    {
      "direction": "GPU neighbor construction and retaining more water state on the GPU",
      "reason": "Exact CPU neighbor searches and synchronous readback waits remain substantial, especially at maximum water resolution.",
      "effort": "Larger follow-up; preserve CPU reference and numerical comparisons."
    },
    {
      "direction": "Incremental support graphs and GPU or tiled sand stock processing",
      "reason": "Local settling and wind indices are now implemented, but hundreds of persistent deposits still increase CPU support/erosion cost over time. The 40-second GPU soak ends with 687 parcels.",
      "effort": "Further work must retain mass, moisture, user edits and support/fracture correctness."
    },
    {
      "direction": "Prewarm shader feature variants",
      "reason": "One-time compilation when a new geometry feature appears can still cause a pause.",
      "effort": "Small-to-moderate follow-up; bound memory use."
